# Jarvis fixture detection — is the lamp on, is the burner lit.
#
# A watcher, not a service anything calls: it subscribes to the hub's frame stream, measures a
# configured region of each frame, and logs a line (and optionally POSTs an alert) when a fixture's
# state changes. The port below serves /health, /fixtures and the calibration preview only.
#
# No model, no GPU, no native library. For a camera that does not move, "is this fixture emitting
# light" is a threshold over a rectangle.
SERVER_ADDRESS=127.0.0.1
SERVER_PORT=9004

# Where the hub is. REQUIRED — a detector that cannot reach the stream has nothing to look at, and
# says so at startup rather than sitting idle looking healthy.
FIXTURE_DETECTION_HUB_URL=http://127.0.0.1:9001
# The durable cursor name the hub remembers this watcher's position under. It matters more here than
# for person detection: a missed stretch of frames is a missed transition, and a fixture's reported
# state is then wrong until the next time somebody touches the switch.
FIXTURE_DETECTION_SUBSCRIPTION=fixture-detection
# Narrows the *stream* to one camera. Usually leave blank and let each fixture name its own source.
FIXTURE_DETECTION_SOURCE=

# WHAT TO WATCH. JSON, because a region is four numbers that only mean anything together and there
# is more than one fixture — see fixtures.example.json, and apps/jarvis/fixture-detection/README.md
# for how to calibrate the thresholds rather than guess them.
#
# A file if one is named (mount it, and it can be edited without a rebuild), inline otherwise.
# Anything unparseable is fatal at startup: a detector watching nothing looks exactly like a working
# one, because silence is what a correct lamp detector produces most of the time.
FIXTURE_DETECTION_DEFINITIONS_FILE=
FIXTURE_DETECTION_DEFINITIONS=

# Where a transition is POSTed. Blank means log only, which is the deliberate difference from person
# detection: transitions are rare and the log line is the record, so alerting is something to switch
# on rather than something failing quietly in the background.
FIXTURE_DETECTION_ALERT_URL=

# LOGGER picks the sinks: console, disk, loki, loki-with-fallback, both (see the root .env.example).
# Worth considering loki-with-fallback here — a transition is reported once and never again, so a log
# line lost to a Loki outage is a state change nobody can recover.
LOGGER=
